<div class="section_content content" id="7685812_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref="LF1574449"><span class="hisdate">4-4-2022</span> by <span class="loclaw">Ord. No. 6.22.22</span></span>]</div><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="16094039"><a alt="359-75A" class="litem_number" href="16094039#16094039" onclick="return false;" title="359-75A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">No person shall park, or move and re-park, a vehicle, nor allow a vehicle to be parked, or moved and re-parked, in any one parking zone as such zones are established in § <a class="xref" guid="7685797" href="7685797#7685797">359-74</a> of this article, for more than two consecutive hours per day between the hours of 8:00 a.m. and 6:00 p.m. on weekdays, except holidays, along any street which has been designated a residential parking permit area pursuant to this article, unless the vehicle is issued a valid parking permit in accordance with this article.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="16094040"><a alt="359-75B" class="litem_number" href="16094040#16094040" onclick="return false;" title="359-75B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Valid residential permit status shall be checked via license plate of the permitted vehicle.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
